========\")\n467:             (println \"Workload W Results:\" (if all-pass? \"SUCCESS\" \"FAILURE\"))\n468:             (println \"================================================================================\")\n469:             (println \"  Hard cap timed out:           \" @timed-out?)\n470:             (println \"  Peer A transfer stalled:      \" @a-stalled?)\n471:             (println \"  Sample count:                 \" sample-count\n472:                      (str \"(valid >= 500: \" valid-run? \", target >= \" target-samples \": \" target-samples-met? \")\"))\n473:             (println \"  p99 round-trip latency:       \" (if (pos? sample-count) (str p99 \"ms\") \"ABSENT\")\n474:                      (str \"(criterion <= 250 ms: \" p99-ok? \")\"))\n475:             (println \"  Peer B replies lost:          \" replies-lost \"(unanswered) +\" @b-lost \"(corrupt)\")\n476:             (println \"  Peer A delivered once:        \" delivered-once?\n477:                      (str \"(deliveries: \" a-deliv-count \", bytes: \" a-deliv-len \", sent: \" @a-sent \")\"))\n478:             (println \"  REPL per-round step advance:  \" repl-advances?\n479:                      (str \"(rounds: \" @owner-round-count \", REPL steps: \" @repl-step-count \")\"))\n480:             (println)\n481: \n482:             ;; Required report records per BRIEF-j6g.md\n483:             (if (pos? sample-count)\n484:               (println \"RECORD p99\" p99 \"ms\")\n485:               (println \"RECORD p99 ABSENT\"))\n486:             (println \"RECORD sample count\" sample-count)\n487:             (println \"RECORD delivered once\" delivered-once?)\n488:             (println \"RECORD per-round step advance\" repl-advances?)\n489: \n490:             (if all-pass?\n491:               (do (println \"PASS workload-w\")\n492:                   {:pass? true\n493:                    :p99 p99\n494:                    :samples sample-count\n495:                    :delivered-once? delivered-once?\n496:                    :repl-advances? repl-advances?\n497:                    :replies-lost replies-lost})\n498:               (do (println \"FAIL workload-w\")\n499:                   {:pass? false\n500:                    :p99 p99\n501:                    :samples sample-count\n502:                    :delivered-once? delivered-once?\n503:                    :repl-advances? repl-advances?\n504:                    :replies-lost replies-lost}))))))))\n505: \n506: \n507: ;; =============================================================================\n508: ;; Deliverable 2: Peer Cross-Host Rows\n509: ;; =============================================================================\n510: \n511: (defn run-cross-host-rows\n512:   \"Verify cross-host listener, dialer, and REPL path reachability rows:\n513:    - Hosts that listen: 127.0.0.1, 0.0.0.0, localhost, ::1; port 0 ephemeral; port collision.\n514:    - Hosts that dial: 127.0.0.1, localhost, [::1]; hostname refused; wss refused.\n515:    - REPL reachability refusals: local reachability failure, reachability failure, disclaimed path.\"\n516:   []\n517:   (println \"================================================================================\")\n518:   (println \"J6g Cross-Host Rows: Running checks...\")\n519:   (println \"================================================================================\")\n520:   (let [w (wake/make-wake)\n521:         passed (atom 0)\n522:         failed (atom 0)\n523:         check! (fn [label ok? detail]\n524:                  (if ok?\n525:                    (do (swap! passed inc)6:    appends what was typed to the input medium, nudges the step owner's wake\n9:    no second state owner, and no line handler evaluates, requests, polls,\n39:   \"The base cadence of the single step owner.  Slow enough to cost nothing\n46:   \"The tick owner's idle curve.  `tick-millis` is the base interval, what a\n214:   \"Create `path` holding `text`, readable by its owner only where the host\n228:        ;; O_CREAT | O_EXCL at 0600 in one call: owner-only from creation,\n233:                   owner-only\n240:                                      [owner-only]))\n636:    the step owner, and the host WebSocket adapter `(connect ...)` attaches\n640:    step owner below is the only thing that steps it.\n1004: (defn- custody-control-step\n1018: (defn- custody-program-step\n1043:    owner's cadence at the base interval, like the driver's own.\"\n1050: (defn step-all\n1051:   \"One tick of the single step owner: the local shell first, then the served\n1106:   \"The tick owner's cadence bit, computed from this tick's own results: true\n1155:   \"How long a host thread may wait for the step owner to finish shutdown.\n1169:    the one step owner still performs the shutdown: `(quit)` stops the shell,\n1171:    one is supplied, is nudged so the step owner runs the quit line at once\n1255: (defn- drain-owner!\n1295: (defn run-owner!\n1296:   \"Serial shell owner shared by the JVM and jolt. Host policy supplies\n1315:         (let [state' (drain-owner! state' server' now sleep!)]\n1333:        \"JVM policy wrapper around the portable serial owner.\"\n1339:         (run-owner! state server headless? #(System/currentTimeMillis)\n1346:        \"The reader parks in `read-line` and appends, nudging the step owner's\n1384:                ;; step owner is joined until it stops, and the explicit stop\n1390:                ;; owner.\n1401:                      ;; other, and the step owner has already exited the process\n1406:                      ;; owner bounds its own shutdown drain (`stop-ticks`)\n1415:      \"One plain-thread owner. Stdin deposits only; EOF deposits (quit).\n1417:       --port; every owner round polls its sockets (headless included) and\n1437:                         (wake/sleep-fds! w ms (:pump adapter)\n1445:              (run-owner! state server headless? #(System/currentTimeMillis)\n1457: ;; cljs (Node): a readline handler that only appends, and o