{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"node_repl","tool":"js","arguments":{"code":"for (var p of ['BRIEF-j6g-fix.md', 'src/cljc/dao/stream/waitset/driver.cljc', 'src/cljc/dao/stream/ws/tcp.cljc']) { try { var s=await fs.readFile(root+'/'+p,'utf8'); show(p,s,1,300); } catch(e) { nodeRepl.write(e.message); } } show('main',main,1235,1348); show('main',main,1410,1455); var driverText=await fs.readFile(root+'/src/cljc/yin/repl/driver.cljc','utf8'); nodeRepl.write(driverText.split('\\n').flatMap((l,i)=>/defn.*repl-step|defn.*submit-line|loop|step-budget/.test(l)?[`${i+1}: ${l}`]:[]).join('\\n'));","title":"Read fix dispatch, sleep implementation, and production owner"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"BRIEF-j6g-fix.md\n1: # J6g fix round: the workload W run hangs — attribute, guard, and re-measure\n2: \n3: (Re-pasted from the orchestrator's dispatch; the agy rounds died twice on\n4: this unit, so this fix round is dispatched to codex per the terminal-state\n5: rule's escalation.)\n6: \n7: ## What happened (the orchestrator's verification run, jupiter, j6ggate18)\n8: \n9: The workload W harness compiled and ran: server listening, peer B\n10: connected and upgraded, peer A connected and upgraded, frame length\n11: 4,194,318 bytes, \"Entering owner round loop...\" — then 100% CPU spin for\n12: 69 minutes, no output flush, no transfer completion. Killed at rc=143.\n13: \n14: The pre-registered criterion (BRIEF-j6g.md, unchanged): A's 4 MiB message\n15: delivered once within a ~60 s window while B samples p99 ≤ 250 ms with\n16: ≥ 600 samples. Nothing measurable was produced.\n17: \n18: ## Your tasks\n19: \n20: 1. **Attribute the spin.** Two hypotheses — distinguish them with reads\n21:    (you cannot run anything):\n22:    (a) a harness defect: `write-all!`'s retry loop (`poll-one fd pollout\n23:    2000` then `send-chunk!`) spins if poll returns writable while send\n24:    answers :would-block, or if the loop never advances off 0; and there\n25:    is no max-runtime guard, so any stall hangs forever.\n26:    (b) a real composition finding: the REPL's owner round serves peer B\n27:    but never drains peer A's 4 MiB transfer (the exact starvation\n28:    workload W exists to expose).\n29:    Read src/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj's write-all!/run-workload-w loop and\n30:    the driver's owner round in src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc (the\n31:    sleep-fds! + step path). State which you conclude, with file:line.\n32: 2. **Fix the harness defects** regardless of (b):\n33:    - a max-runtime guard: the whole workload terminates with a FAILURE\n34:      report (p99 absent, samples counted, elapsed) after a hard cap\n35:      (5 minutes), never hanging;\n36:    - the write-all! loop gets a no-progress guard: N consecutive\n37:      :would-block polls without a byte advancing = transfer stalled →\n38:      report and abort the transfer leg (this is data: the criterion\n39:      failing, honestly measured);\n40:    - the sampler flushes its running p99/sample-count to stdout every\n41:      10 s so a stuck run leaves evidence.\n42: 3. **If (b) is your conclusion** (the adapter starves A): do NOT patch\n43:    the adapter — report it as the finding with the reads that support it.\n44:    The Architect rules on adapter changes.\n45: 4. cljstyle clean; no collab/ path in comments.\n46: \n47: ## Reporting\n48: \n49: Write BRIEF-j6g-fix-findings.md in this workspace with: the attribution,\n50: the guards added, and what the next verification run should show under\n51: each hypothesis.\n52: ENOENT: no such file or directory, open '/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-j6g/src/cljc/dao/stream/waitset/driver.cljc'ENOENT: no such file or directory, open '/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-j6g/src/cljc/dao/stream/ws/tcp.cljc'main\n1235: \n1236: (defn shutdown-tick\n1237:   \"One tick of the bounded shutdown drain (r3 1.12, residual 4), the tick\n1238:    every host's drain loop calls: the custody control plane keeps running --\n1239:    the holders' local stop latch is set here, at drain entry, on every host,\n1240:    including paths that reached the drain without another normal `step-all`\n1241:    -- and the head board and the endpoint drain (an absent endpoint drains\n1242:    nothing and answers stopped).  No custody program step runs: program\n1243:    execution stays stopped once the shell has.  Returns\n1244:    `[state server lines stopped?]`; the budget (`stop-ticks`) and the exit\n1245:    condition (`shutdown-enter?`, `shutdown-drained?`) are the caller's.\"\n1246:   [state server now]\n1247:   (let [state (custody-control-step (custody-stop state))]\n1248:     (stop-tick state server now)))\n1249: \n1250: \n1251: ;; =============================================================================\n1252: ;; clj: a reader thread that only appends, and one owned poller thread\n1253: ;; =============================================================================\n1254: \n1255: (defn- drain-owner!\n1256:   \"The shell has quit, so the head board, the endpoint and the custody\n1257:         control plane stop before the host exits: ask the board and the\n1258:         endpoint once, then keep stepping all three until the endpoint has\n1259:         stopped AND the board owes nothing AND custody owes no further\n1260:         control write (`shutdown-drained?`), or the bounded budget runs\n1261:         out.  The drain is entered at all only when one of them owes\n1262:         something (`shutdown-enter?` -- a shell with no endpoint enters it\n1263:         on owed custody writes alone).  A connected client must observe the\n1264:         ended answer, not the bare close a process exit would leave behind.\n1265:         Each drain round lasts at least the base interval of wall time,\n1266:         however many early wakes readiness causes; the budget counts rounds,\n1267:         so the drain is at least `tick-millis x stop-ticks` of wall time.\n1268:         The custody control plane steps on every one of its ticks\n1269:         (`shutdown-tick`); the state it reaches is durable in the progress\n1270:         journal, so what the budget leaves outstanding is a restart's to\n1271:         resend.  Answers the drained state.\"\n1272:   [state server now sleep!]\n1273:   (if (shutdown-enter? state server)\n1274:     (loop [state (update state :repl repl.dht/stop!)\n1275:            server (some-> server serve/stop!)\n1276:            remaining stop-ticks]\n1277:       (let [[state' server' lines _stopped?]\n1278:             (shutdown-tick state server (now))]\n1279:         (doseq [line lines]\n1280:           (println line))\n1281:         (flush)\n1282:         (cond\n1283:           (shutdown-drained? state' server') state'\n1284:           (zero? remaining) (do (println stop-timeout-text) state')\n1285:           :else (let [round-end (+ (now) tick-millis)]\n1286:                   ;; a sleep readiness ends early pumps, then sleeps the\n1287:                   ;; rest: an early wake cannot spend a round (R17)\n1288:                   (loop []\n1289:                     (sleep! (max 0 (- round-end (now))))\n1290:                     (when (< (now) round-end) (recur)))\n1291:                   (recur state' server' (dec remaining))))))\n1292:     state))\n1293: \n1294: \n1295: (defn run-owner!\n1296:   \"Serial shell owner shared by the JVM and jolt. Host policy supplies\n1297:    clock, interruptible sleep and status-aware exit. No producer evaluates.\"\n1298:   [state server headless? now sleep! exit!]\n1299:   (loop [state state\n1300:          server server\n1301:          cadence (cadence/init default-cadence)]\n1302:     (let [[state' server' lines] (step-all state server\n1303:                                            (now))]\n1304:       (doseq [line lines]\n1305:         (println line))\n1306:       (flush)\n1307:       (if (:running? state')\n1308:         (do (when (and (not headless?) (prompt-owed? state state' lines))\n1309:               (do (print prompt) (flush)))\n1310:             (let [{:keys [cadence-state sleep-ms]}\n1311:                   (cadence/cadence-step cadence\n1312:                                         (moved? state' server' lines))]\n1313:               (sleep! sleep-ms)\n1314:               (recur state' server' cadence-state)))\n1315:         (let [state' (drain-owner! state' server' now sleep!)]\n1316:           (println)\n1317:           (close-index-store! state')\n1318:           (flush)\n1319:           (exit! (exit-status state')))))))\n1320: \n1321: \n1322: #?(:cljd\n1323:    nil\n1324:    :jolt nil\n1325:    :clj\n1326:    (do\n1327:      (defn- print-prompt!\n1328:        []\n1329:        (print prompt)\n1330:        (flush))\n1331: \n1332:      (defn poll-loop!\n1333:        \"JVM policy wrapper around the portable serial owner.\"\n1334:        ([state server headless?]\n1335:         (poll-loop! state server headless? #(.halt (Runtime/getRuntime) 0)))\n1336:        ([state server headless? exit!]\n1337:         (poll-loop! state server headless? exit! (wake/make-wake)))\n1338:        ([state server headless? exit! w]\n1339:         (run-owner! state server headless? #(System/currentTimeMillis)\n1340:                     #(wake/sleep! w %)\n1341:                     (fn [status]\n1342:                       (if (zero? status) (exit!)\n1343:                           (.halt (Runtime/getRuntime) (int status)))))))\n1344: \n1345:      (defn- read-loop!\n1346:        \"The reader parks in `read-line` and appends, nudging the step owner's\n1347:         wake: a typed line ends the idle sleep at once.  It reads no state.\"\n1348:        [input w]main\n1410:              (.halt (Runtime/getRuntime) 0)))))))\n1411: \n1412: \n1413: #?(:jolt\n1414:    (defn -main\n1415:      \"One plain-thread owner. Stdin deposits only; EOF deposits (quit).\n1416:       One host WebSocket instance serves the shell, the head board and\n1417:       --port; every owner round polls its sockets (headless included) and\n1418:       the instance is closed before exit, however the drain ended.\n1419:       Saved flags persist in the node directory, as on the JVM (J4d):\n1420:       --reset forgets them and --no-state neither reads nor writes them.\"\n1421:      [& args]\n1422:      (let [adapter (host/websocket)\n1423:            started (startup args {:persist? true :adapter adapter})]\n1424:        (when (contains? started :exit) (exit-with! started))\n1425:        (if-some [refusal (:refusal started)]\n1426:          (refuse! refusal)\n1427:          (let [{:keys [opts state server]} started\n1428:                headless? (boolean (:headless? opts))\n1429:                eof? (atom false)\n1430:                w (wake/make-wake)\n1431:                line! (fn [line]\n1432:                        (if (nil? line)\n1433:                          (do (reset! eof? true)\n1434:                              (driver/submit-line! (:input state) \"(quit)\"))\n1435:                          (driver/submit-line! (:input state) line)))\n1436:                sleep! (fn [ms]\n1437:                         (wake/sleep-fds! w ms (:pump adapter)\n1438:                                          (when-not (or headless? @eof?) line!)))]\n1439:            (doseq [line (banner opts)] (println line))\n1440:            (when-not headless? (print prompt))\n1441:            (flush)\n1442:            ;; the exit status leaves through System/exit, which skips the\n1443:            ;; finally, so the exit path closes the instance itself too\n1444:            (try\n1445:              (run-owner! state server headless? #(System/currentTimeMillis)\n1446:                          sleep! (fn [status]\n1447:                                   ((:close-host! adapter))\n1448:                                   (wake/close! w)\n1449:                                   (flush)\n1450:                                   (System/exit status)))\n1451:              (finally\n1452:                ((:close-host! adapter))\n1453:                (wake/close! w))))))))\n1454: \n1455: 12:    It never loops on `blocked`, and it owns no promise, future, callback, atom,\n98: (defn submit-line!\n137:   (loop [remaining input-budget\n579: (defn repl-step\n580:   \"Advance the REPL once.  Called by exactly one ticker per host; never loops on"}],"_meta":{"codex/nodeReplExecutionDurationMs":15},"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
