{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"node_repl","tool":"js","arguments":{"code":"nodeRepl.write(entries.filter(p=>/waitset\\/driver|ws\\/(tcp|jolt)|jolt\\/(ffi|socket\\/native|io_poller)|jolt_workload|j6g/.test(p) && !/\\.git\\/|node_modules\\//.test(p))); show('driver',driverText,570,655); show('main',main,1040,1108);","title":"Locate native transport files and inspect REPL stepping"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"[\n  'BRIEF-j6g-fix.md',\n  'test/dao/stream/waitset/driver_test.clj',\n  'test/dao/stream/waitset/driver_test.cljd',\n  'test/dao/stream/waitset/driver_test.cljs',\n  'src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/jolt.jolt',\n  'src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/tcp.jolt',\n  'src/jolt/dao/stream/waitset/driver.jolt',\n  'src/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj',\n  'src/cljs/dao/stream/waitset/driver.cljs',\n  'src/cljd/dao/stream/waitset/driver.cljd',\n  'src/clj/dao/stream/waitset/driver.clj'\n]driver\n570:           (assoc :queued (vec rest-lines))\n571:           (submit-remote line requeue-line)))\n572:     state))\n573: \n574: \n575: ;; =============================================================================\n576: ;; The step\n577: ;; =============================================================================\n578: \n579: (defn repl-step\n580:   \"Advance the REPL once.  Called by exactly one ticker per host; never loops on\n581:    `:dao.stream/blocked`.  `now` is the host's clock reading, recorded but not\n582:    waited on: this layer has no deadline of its own.\"\n583:   [state now]\n584:   (let [state (assoc state :last-tick now)\n585:         state (retry-unsent state)\n586:         ;; Completions and lifecycle are observed before this tick's lines are\n587:         ;; handled, so a `(connect …)` typed in the same tick as the drop that\n588:         ;; makes it legal sees the terminal fact rather than being told the\n589:         ;; shell is already connected.\n590:         state (poll-remote state now)\n591:         state (observe-connection state)\n592:         [state lines] (drain-input state)\n593:         state (reduce handle-line state lines)]\n594:     (release-queue state)))\n595: main\n1040: (defn- custody-owed?\n1041:   \"True while the shell's custody composition owes a control-plane\n1042:    write (compose/owed-control-write?): a pending write keeps the tick\n1043:    owner's cadence at the base interval, like the driver's own.\"\n1044:   [state]\n1045:   (if-some [c (custody-of state)]\n1046:     (compose/owed-control-write? c)\n1047:     false))\n1048: \n1049: \n1050: (defn step-all\n1051:   \"One tick of the single step owner: the local shell first, then the served\n1052:    endpoint, against the same shell value.  A DHT index store's node is stepped\n1053:    first (yin.repl.dht/step): its lines print before the shell's, a\n1054:    hydration still outstanding leaves every typed line waiting in the\n1055:    input medium, and a refused one stops the shell.  The custody control\n1056:    plane is stepped next, before the refusal and admission branches, so\n1057:    renewals, pending releases and request retries continue during\n1058:    hydration and past a refusal.  A `--port` process\n1059:    serves one shared shell, as v1's atom made it: the driver evaluates this\n1060:    tick's local\n1061:    lines first, so a definition typed at the local prompt is already in the\n1062:    shell the endpoint evaluates remote requests against in the same tick, and\n1063:    the endpoint's shell (remote definitions included) is threaded back\n1064:    before the next tick.  The custody program step follows the driver's own\n1065:    step and precedes the endpoint's; once the shell has stopped it is\n1066:    replaced by the stop latch, so no custody program call runs after\n1067:    `:running?` turns false.  A require parked on a closure load the node\n1068:    ended this tick is re-checked once, before any typed line, with no line\n1069:    of its own (yin.repl/recheck-on-tick, yin.vm.linker.dht.md 8.2),\n1070:    and linker progress resumes a parked run (7.5): its text prints after the\n1071:    node's lines.  Returns `[state server lines]`;\n1072:    the caller only prints.\"\n1073:   [state server now]\n1074:   (let [[repl dht-lines events] (repl.dht/step (:repl state) now)\n1075:         state (custody-control-step (assoc state :repl repl))]\n1076:     (cond\n1077:       (repl.dht/refusal repl)\n1078:       [(custody-stop (assoc state :running? false)) server dht-lines]\n1079: \n1080:       (not (repl.dht/admitting? repl))\n1081:       [state server dht-lines]\n1082: \n1083:       :else\n1084:       (let [[repl rechecked] (shell/recheck-on-tick (:repl state) events)\n1085:             dht-lines (cond-> dht-lines\n1086:                         (seq rechecked) (conj rechecked))\n1087:             state (assoc state :repl repl)\n1088:             stepped (driver/repl-step state now)\n1089:             stepped (if (:running? stepped)\n1090:                       (custody-program-step stepped)\n1091:                       (custody-stop stepped))\n1092:             [entries state'] (driver/take-outbox stepped)\n1093:             server' (when server\n1094:                       (serve/step (assoc-in server [:repl] (:repl state'))\n1095:                                   now))\n1096:             [server-entries server''] (if server'\n1097:                                         (serve/take-outbox server')\n1098:                                         [[] nil])\n1099:             state'' (if server'' (assoc state' :repl (:repl server'')) state')]\n1100:         [state'' server'' (into dht-lines\n1101:                                 (map entry-text)\n1102:                                 (into (vec entries) server-entries))]))))\n1103: \n1104: \n1105: (defn moved?\n1106:   \"The tick owner's cadence bit, computed from this tick's own results: true\n1107:    when there are lines to print, when the endpoint reports movement (a\n1108:    woken probe, a published notice), or when either composition still owes a"}],"_meta":{"codex/nodeReplExecutionDurationMs":13},"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The current harness already has partial guards, but they only run between owner rounds. They cannot fire if a REPL step or I/O pump never returns. Also, `write-all!` only sends A’s upgrade request; the large-frame path uses `write-some!`. I’m tracing that path before attributing the spin."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"node_repl","tool":"js","arguments":{"code":"for (var p of ['src/jolt/dao/stream/waitset/driver.jolt','src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/tcp.jolt']) { var s=await fs.readFile(root+'/'+p,'utf8'); show(p,s,1,380); } var joltText=await fs.readFile(root+'/src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/jolt.jolt','utf8'); nodeRepl.write(joltText.split('\\n').flatMap((l,i)=>/defn|loop|poll!|read!|write!|pump|recv|send|budget/.test(l)?[`${i+1}: ${l}`]:[]).join('\\n'));","title":"Trace jolt waitset polling and raw socket semantics"},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"node_repl","tool":"js","arguments":{"code":"for (var p of ['src/jolt/dao/stream/waitset/driver.jolt','src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/tcp.jolt']) { var s=await fs.readFile(root+'/'+p,'utf8'); show(p,s,1,380); } var joltText=await fs.readFile(root+'/src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/jolt.jolt','utf8'); nodeRepl.write(joltText.split('\\n').flatMap((l,i)=>/defn|loop|poll!|read!|write!|pump|recv|send|budget/.test(l)?[`${i+1}: ${l}`]:[]).join('\\n'));","title":"Trace jolt waitset polling and raw socket semantics"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"src/jolt/dao/stream/waitset/driver.jolt\n1: (ns dao.stream.waitset.driver\n2:   \"Jolt wait-set wake policy: a nonblocking self-pipe carrying contentless\n3:    tokens. No interpreter state or dispatch lives here. Plain-thread waits\n4:    use the poller's monotonic deadline; stdin and socket waits multiplex the\n5:    same pipe with fd 0 and a pump's interest descriptors through jolt's\n6:    native poll binding, on the one owner thread. No reader thread.\n7: \n8:    Stdin is read raw from fd 0 into a driver-owned line buffer (plan v2 A1),\n9:    one read(2) per round and only after poll reported fd 0 ready, so the\n10:    read never waits. Complete lines are deposited; a partial line stays\n11:    buffered and never blocks the owner; a zero-length read is end of input.\n12:    Chez's buffered System/in is never read, so no byte is split between two\n13:    readers.\"\n14:   (:require [dao.host.text :as text]\n15:             [jolt.ffi :as ffi]\n16:             [jolt.io-poller :as poller]\n17:             [jolt.socket.native :as native]))\n18: \n19: \n20: (ffi/load-library)\n21: (ffi/defcfn c-pipe \"pipe\" [:pointer] :int)\n22: \n23: \n24: (def ^:private stdin-chunk 4096)\n25: \n26: \n27: (defn make-wake\n28:   []\n29:   (let [fds (ffi/alloc 8)]\n30:     (try\n31:       (when (neg? (c-pipe fds))\n32:         (throw (ex-info \"wake pipe creation failed\" {:errno (ffi/errno)})))\n33:       (let [r (ffi/read fds :int 0) w (ffi/read fds :int 4)]\n34:         (poller/nonblock! r)\n35:         (poller/nonblock! w)\n36:         ;; :stdin is the partial line held between rounds (bytes after the\n37:         ;; last newline), owned by this wake's one owner thread\n38:         {:read r :write w :stdin (atom (byte-array 0))})\n39:       (finally (ffi/free fds)))))\n40: \n41: \n42: (defn close!\n43:   [wake]\n44:   (poller/forget! (:read wake))\n45:   (poller/c-close (:read wake))\n46:   (poller/c-close (:write wake))\n47:   nil)\n48: \n49: \n50: (defn nudge!\n51:   [wake]\n52:   (let [b (ffi/alloc 1)]\n53:     (try\n54:       (ffi/write b :uint8 1)\n55:       (loop []\n56:         (let [n (poller/c-write (:write wake) b 1) e (ffi/errno)]\n57:           (cond\n58:             (= n 1) nil\n59:             (poller/eintr? e) (recur)\n60:             (poller/eagain? e) nil ; a full pipe already owes a wake\n61:             :else (throw (ex-info \"wake pipe write failed\" {:errno e})))))\n62:       (finally (ffi/free b)))))\n63: \n64: \n65: (defn- drain!\n66:   [wake]\n67:   (let [b (ffi/alloc 256)]\n68:     (try\n69:       (loop [woken? false]\n70:         (let [n (poller/c-read (:read wake) b 256) e (ffi/errno)]\n71:           (cond\n72:             (pos? n) (recur true)\n73:             (poller/eintr? e) (recur woken?)\n74:             (poller/eagain? e) woken?\n75:             :else (throw (ex-info \"wake pipe read failed\" {:errno e :read n})))))\n76:       (finally (ffi/free b)))))\n77: \n78: \n79: (defn sleep!\n80:   [wake sleep-ms]\n81:   (poller/wait-ready (:read wake) :read (poller/deadline-ms sleep-ms))\n82:   (drain! wake))\n83: \n84: \n85: ;; =============================================================================\n86: ;; Stdin lines\n87: ;; =============================================================================\n88: \n89: (defn- concat-bytes\n90:   [a b]\n91:   (let [na (alength a) nb (alength b) out (byte-array (+ na nb))]\n92:     (dotimes [i na] (aset out i (aget a i)))\n93:     (dotimes [i nb] (aset out (+ na i) (aget b i)))\n94:     out))\n95: \n96: \n97: (defn- slice\n98:   [bs start end]\n99:   (let [out (byte-array (- end start))]\n100:     (dotimes [i (- end start)] (aset out i (aget bs (+ start i))))\n101:     out))\n102: \n103: \n104: (defn- decode-line\n105:   \"The text of line bytes `bs` (newline excluded), one trailing CR dropped\n106:    as the JVM's readLine does. Ill-formed UTF-8 falls back to jolt's\n107:    lossy decode rather than losing the line.\"\n108:   [bs]\n109:   (let [n (alength bs)\n110:         n (if (and (pos? n) (= 13 (aget bs (dec n)))) (dec n) n)]\n111:     (try\n112:       (text/utf8-decode bs 0 n)\n113:       (catch Throwable _\n114:         (let [p (ffi/alloc (max 1 n))]\n115:           (try (ffi/write-array p bs 0 n)\n116:                (ffi/read-bytes p n)\n117:                (finally (ffi/free p))))))))\n118: \n119: \n120: (defn- deposit-lines!\n121:   \"Append `chunk` to the held partial line and deposit every complete line\n122:    through `line!`, keeping the remainder.\"\n123:   [wake chunk line!]\n124:   (let [bs (concat-bytes @(:stdin wake) chunk)\n125:         n (alength bs)]\n126:     (loop [start 0 i 0]\n127:       (cond\n128:         (= i n) (reset! (:stdin wake) (slice bs start n))\n129:         (= 10 (aget bs i)) (do (line! (decode-line (slice bs start i)))\n130:                                (recur (inc i) (inc i)))\n131:         :else (recur start (inc i))))))\n132: \n133: \n134: (defn- end-of-input!\n135:   \"Deposit a held unterminated last line, as read-line answers it, then\n136:    nil.\"\n137:   [wake line!]\n138:   (let [held @(:stdin wake)]\n139:     (reset! (:stdin wake) (byte-array 0))\n140:     (when (pos? (alength held)) (line! (decode-line held)))\n141:     (line! nil)))\n142: \n143: \n144: (defn- read-stdin!\n145:   \"One read(2) of fd 0, which poll reported ready. Answers true when it\n146:    deposited or reached end of input.\"\n147:   [wake line!]\n148:   (let [buf (ffi/alloc stdin-chunk)]\n149:     (try\n150:       (let [n (poller/c-read 0 buf stdin-chunk) e (ffi/errno)]\n151:         (cond\n152:           (pos? n) (do (deposit-lines! wake (ffi/read-array buf n) line!) true)\n153:           (and (neg? n) (or (poller/eintr? e) (poller/eagain? e))) false\n154:           ;; zero, or a descriptor that cannot be read (closed fd 0): end\n155:           :else (do (end-of-input! wake line!) true)))\n156:       (finally (ffi/free buf)))))\n157: \n158: \n159: ;; =============================================================================\n160: ;; One owner round\n161: ;; =============================================================================\n162: \n163: (defn sleep-fds!\n164:   \"One owner round's wait (plan v2 A1): poll the wake pipe, fd 0 (when\n165:    `line!` is given) and `pump`'s interest descriptors (when `pump` is\n166:    given) until one is ready or the earlier of `sleep-ms` and the pump's\n167:    `:deadline` (`jolt.io-poller/clock-ms`; nil, or a pump without one, is\n168:    the cadence alone) passes; then drain the wake pipe, run one\n169:    `(:pump! pump)` turn over the observed `[[fd revents] ...]` (every\n170:    round; `[]` after a timeout), then deposit stdin lines through `line!`\n171:    (nil at end of input). A deadline already due still polls once, with a\n172:    zero timeout, so readiness seen then reaches the same `pump!` turn as\n173:    the expiry. Never evaluates. Answers truthy when anything was woken,\n174:    moved or deposited.\"\n175:   [wake sleep-ms pump line!]\n176:   (let [interest (if pump (vec ((:interest pump))) [])\n177:         base (if line! 2 1)\n178:         n (+ base (count interest))\n179:         fds (native/alloc-pollfds n)\n180:         cadence (poller/deadline-ms sleep-ms)\n181:         due (when-let [f (:deadline pump)] (f))\n182:         deadline (if due (min due cadence) cadence)]\n183:     (try\n184:       (native/init-pollfd! fds 0 (:read wake) native/pollin)\n185:       (when line! (native/init-pollfd! fds 1 0 native/pollin))\n186:       (dotimes [i (count interest)]\n187:         (let [[fd events] (nth interest i)]\n188:           (native/init-pollfd! fds (+ base i) fd events)))\n189:       (loop []\n190:         (let [remaining (max 0 (long (Math/ceil (- deadline (poller/clock-ms)))))\n191:               [rc e] (native/c-poll fds n remaining)]\n192:           (cond\n193:             (and (neg? rc) (native/eintr? e)) (recur)\n194:             (neg? rc) (throw (ex-info \"owner poll failed\" {:errno e}))\n195:             :else nil)))\n196:       (let [ready (vec (keep (fn [i]\n197:                                (let [rev (native/pollfd-revents fds (+ base i))]\n198:                                  (when (pos? rev) [(first (nth interest i)) rev])))\n199:                              (range (count interest))))\n200:             woken? (drain! wake)\n201:             progressed? (when pump (:progressed? ((:pump! pump) ready)))\n202:             stdin? (when (and line! (pos? (native/pollfd-revents fds 1)))\n203:                      (read-stdin! wake line!))]\n204:         (or woken? progressed? stdin?))\n205:       (finally (ffi/free fds)))))\n206: \n207: \n208: (defn sleep-input!\n209:   \"Wait for a nudge, stdin, or the cadence deadline. `line!` only deposits\n210:    lines (nil at EOF). Never evaluate from this seam.\"\n211:   [wake sleep-ms line!]\n212:   (sleep-fds! wake sleep-ms nil line!))\n213: src/jolt/dao/stream/ws/tcp.jolt\n1: (ns dao.stream.ws.tcp\n2:   \"Jolt-only TCP substrate under the native WebSocket host adapter (J6d,\n3:    plan v2 §3; docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §9.3): nonblocking\n4:    stream sockets over `jolt.socket.native`, never the `jolt.socket` java.net\n5:    shim, whose write path waits for the socket to drain.\n6: \n7:    Every descriptor made here is nonblocking and close-on-exec, and carries\n8:    SIGPIPE suppression (SO_NOSIGPIPE on macOS from `new-socket` and\n9:    `guard-accepted!`, MSG_NOSIGNAL per send on Linux), so a write to a peer\n10:    that has gone answers an error instead of ending the process. An accepted\n11:    descriptor is made nonblocking explicitly: Linux does not inherit the\n12:    listener's mode.\n13: \n14:    Nothing here waits. Connect answers `:connecting` on EINPROGRESS and\n15:    `connect-result` reads SO_ERROR once the descriptor is writable; recv and\n16:    send are one transfer each (EINTR retried) answering data, never throwing\n17:    for a socket condition. End of stream, reset and broken pipe are distinct\n18:    classes.\n19: \n20:    Names: `parse-address` accepts IPv4 and IPv6 literals and `localhost`\n21:    (mapped to 127.0.0.1) and never calls the resolver (plan v2 A6); any\n22:    other host is `{:error :host-name-unsupported}`.\"\n23:   (:require\n24:     [clojure.string :as str]\n25:     [jolt.ffi :as ffi]\n26:     [jolt.socket.native :as native]))\n27: \n28: \n29: ;; =============================================================================\n30: ;; Addresses (plan v2 A6)\n31: ;; =============================================================================\n32: \n33: (defn- literal\n34:   \"{:family :ip} for the numeric literal `s`, the ip in its canonical\n35:    presentation form, or nil. inet_pton only; no resolver.\"\n36:   [s]\n37:   (some (fn [family]\n38:           (when-let [[sa _] (native/make-sockaddr family s 0)]\n39:             (try {:family family, :ip (native/sockaddr-ip sa)}\n40:                  (finally (ffi/free sa)))))\n41:         [native/af-inet native/af-inet6]))\n42: \n43: \n44: (defn- literal-shaped?\n45:   \"Whether `s` reads as an attempted address literal rather than a name:\n46:    only digits and dots, or any colon.\"\n47:   [s]\n48:   (boolean (or (str/includes? s \":\") (re-matches #\"[0-9.]+\" s))))\n49: \n50: \n51: (defn parse-address\n52:   \"`{:family :ip :port}` for `host` and `port`, or `{:error kind}` with kind\n53:    `:host-name-unsupported` (a name other than localhost), `:malformed-address`\n54:    (a literal inet_pton refuses) or `:invalid-port`. A bracketed IPv6 literal\n55:    (`[::1]`) is accepted. Never resolves: names are decidable here and now.\"\n56:   [host port]\n57:   (let [h (when (string? host)\n58:             (if (and (str/starts-with? host \"[\") (str/ends-with? host \"]\"))\n59:               (subs host 1 (dec (count host)))\n60:               host))]\n61:     (cond\n62:       (not (and (int? port) (<= 0 port 65535))) {:error :invalid-port}\n63:       (or (nil? h) (str/blank? h)) {:error :malformed-address}\n64:       (= \"localhost\" (str/lower-case h)) {:family native/af-inet, :ip \"127.0.0.1\", :port port}\n65:       :else (if-let [lit (literal h)]\n66:               (assoc lit :port port)\n67:               {:error (if (literal-shaped? h) :malformed-address :host-name-unsupported)}))))\n68: \n69: \n70: (defn- with-sockaddr\n71:   \"(f sa len) over a fresh sockaddr for a parsed address, freed after.\"\n72:   [{:keys [family ip port]} f]\n73:   (let [[sa len] (native/make-sockaddr family ip port)]\n74:     (try (f sa len) (finally (ffi/free sa)))))\n75: \n76: \n77: ;; =============================================================================\n78: ;; Error classes\n79: ;; =============================================================================\n80: \n81: (defn error-class\n82:   \"The class of socket error `e`: :reset, :broken-pipe, :refused,\n83:    :not-connected or :other. A reset and a broken pipe are both a peer that\n84:    has gone; they stay distinct for diagnostics.\"\n85:   [e]\n86:   (cond\n87:     (= e native/econnreset) :reset\n88:     (and native/epipe (= e native/epipe)) :broken-pipe\n89:     (= e native/econnrefused) :refused\n90:     (= e native/enotconn) :not-connected\n91:     :else :other))\n92: \n93: \n94: (defn- failure\n95:   [kind e]\n96:   {:error kind, :class (error-class e), :errno e, :message (native/error-message e)})\n97: \n98: \n99: ;; =============================================================================\n100: ;; Descriptors\n101: ;; =============================================================================\n102: \n103: (defn close!\n104:   \"Close `fd` once. EINTR is not retried: on Linux the descriptor is released\n105:    whatever close answers, and a retry could close a reused number.\"\n106:   [fd]\n107:   (native/c-close fd)\n108:   nil)\n109: \n110: \n111: (defn shutdown!\n112:   \"shutdown(2) `fd` for :read, :write or :both; answers nil, ignoring\n113:    ENOTCONN (a peer that already went).\"\n114:   [fd how]\n115:   (native/c-shutdown fd (case how :read native/shut-rd :write native/shut-wr native/shut-rdwr))\n116:   nil)\n117: \n118: \n119: (defn- nonblocking!\n120:   \"O_NONBLOCK on `fd`; answers nil or the errno it failed with.\"\n121:   [fd]\n122:   (let [[r e] (native/set-blocking! fd false)]\n123:     (when (neg? r) e)))\n124: \n125: \n126: (defn- open-socket\n127:   \"A fresh nonblocking, close-on-exec stream socket of `family`, or a\n128:    failure map.\"\n129:   [family]\n130:   (let [fd (try (native/new-socket family) (catch Throwable _ nil))]\n131:     (if (nil? fd)\n132:       {:error :socket-failed}\n133:       (if-let [e (nonblocking! fd)]\n134:         (do (close! fd) (failure :socket-failed e))\n135:         {:fd fd}))))\n136: \n137: \n138: (defn local-port\n139:   \"The port `fd` is bound to (the kernel's pick after port 0), or -1.\"\n140:   [fd]\n141:   (native/local-port fd))\n142: \n143: \n144: (defn nonblocking?\n145:   \"Whether `fd` has O_NONBLOCK set, read back with F_GETFL.\"\n146:   [fd]\n147:   (let [[flags _] (native/c-fcntl fd 3 0)]\n148:     (and (not (neg? flags))\n149:          (pos? (bit-and flags (if (= native/os :macos) 0x4 0x800))))))\n150: \n151: \n152: ;; =============================================================================\n153: ;; Listener\n154: ;; =============================================================================\n155: \n156: (defn listen!\n157:   \"A nonblocking listener on the parsed `addr` (`parse-address`):\n158:    `{:fd :port}` with the actual port, or a failure map (`:error`\n159:    `:bind-failed`/`:listen-failed`/`:socket-failed`). The descriptor is\n160:    closed on failure.\"\n161:   ([addr] (listen! addr 128))\n162:   ([addr backlog]\n163:    (let [{:keys [fd] :as opened} (open-socket (:family addr))]\n164:      (if-not fd\n165:        opened\n166:        (let [_ (native/set-listener-reuse! fd)\n167:              [rb eb] (with-sockaddr addr (fn [sa len] (native/c-bind fd sa len)))]\n168:          (if (neg? rb)\n169:            (do (close! fd) (failure :bind-failed eb))\n170:            (let [[rl el] (native/c-listen fd backlog)]\n171:              (if (neg? rl)\n172:                (do (close! fd) (failure :listen-failed el))\n173:                {:fd fd, :port (local-port fd)}))))))))\n174: \n175: \n176: ;; One accept(2) each; the test seam (redefined by the probe only).\n177: (defn accept-once\n178:   [lfd sa lenp]\n179:   (native/c-accept lfd sa lenp))\n180: \n181: \n182: (defn accept!\n183:   \"One nonblocking accept on listener `lfd`: `{:fd :peer}` for a connection,\n184:    explicitly nonblocking, close-on-exec, SIGPIPE-suppressed and\n185:    TCP_NODELAY; `:would-block` when none is pending; or a failure map\n186:    (`:error :accept-failed`). EINTR is retried.\"\n187:   [lfd]\n188:   (let [[sa lenp] (native/alloc-sockaddr)]\n189:     (try\n190:       (loop []\n191:         (let [[fd e] (accept-once lfd sa lenp)]\n192:           (cond\n193:             (not (neg? fd))\n194:             (if-let [e (nonblocking! fd)]\n195:               (do (close! fd) (failure :accept-failed e))\n196:               (do (native/guard-accepted! fd)\n197:                   (native/set-int-option! fd native/ipproto-tcp native/tcp-nodelay 1)\n198:                   {:fd fd\n199:                    :peer {:family (native/sockaddr-family sa)\n200:                           :ip (native/sockaddr-ip sa)\n201:                           :port (native/sockaddr-port sa)}}))\n202:             (native/eintr? e) (recur)\n203:             (native/eagain? e) :would-block\n204:             :else (failure :accept-failed e))))\n205:       (finally (ffi/free sa) (ffi/free lenp)))))\n206: \n207: \n208: ;; =============================================================================\n209: ;; Dialer\n210: ;; =============================================================================\n211: \n212: (defn connect!\n213:   \"Start a nonblocking connect to the parsed `addr`: `{:fd :state\n214:    :connected}`, `{:fd :state :connecting}` (EINPROGRESS: wait for the\n215:    descriptor to be writable, then `connect-result`), or a failure map\n216:    (`:error :connect-failed`), the descriptor closed. Never waits.\"\n217:   [addr]\n218:   (let [{:keys [fd] :as opened} (open-socket (:family addr))]\n219:     (if-not fd\n220:       opened\n221:       (let [[r e] (with-sockaddr addr (fn [sa len] (native/c-connect fd sa len)))]\n222:         (native/set-int-option! fd native/ipproto-tcp native/tcp-nodelay 1)\n223:         (cond\n224:           (not (neg? r)) {:fd fd, :state :connected}\n225:           ;; an interrupted connect carries on asynchronously, as EINPROGRESS\n226:           (or (native/connect-pending? e) (native/eintr? e)) {:fd fd, :state :connecting}\n227:           :else (do (close! fd) (failure :connect-failed e)))))))\n228: \n229: \n230: (defn connect-result\n231:   \"The outcome of a connect that answered `:connecting`, read once its\n232:    descriptor is writable: `:connected` or a failure map (`:error\n233:    :connect-failed`, from SO_ERROR). Does not close the descriptor.\"\n234:   [fd]\n235:   (let [e (native/pending-error fd)]\n236:     (cond\n237:       (zero? e) :connected\n238:       (neg? e) {:error :connect-failed, :class :other, :errno -1, :message \"SO_ERROR unreadable\"}\n239:       :else (failure :connect-failed e))))\n240: \n241: \n242: ;; =============================================================================\n243: ;; Transfers\n244: ;; =============================================================================\n245: \n246: ;; One system call each, answering [result errno]. The chunk functions call\n247: ;; them through these vars, which is the test-only indirection the J6d probe\n248: ;; redefines to script short, EAGAIN and failing transfers. There is no\n249: ;; production fault mode.\n250: \n251: (defn recv-once\n252:   [fd buf n]\n253:   (native/c-recv fd buf n 0))\n254: \n255: \n256: (defn send-once\n257:   [fd buf n]\n258:   (native/c-send fd buf n native/msg-nosignal))\n259: \n260: \n261: (defn recv-chunk!\n262:   \"One recv of at most `cap` bytes into native `buf`: `{:n n}` (n > 0),\n263:    `:eof`, `:would-block`, or a failure map (`:error :recv-failed`, `:class`\n264:    :reset for ECONNRESET). EINTR is retried.\"\n265:   [fd buf cap]\n266:   (loop []\n267:     (let [[n e] (recv-once fd buf cap)]\n268:       (cond\n269:         (pos? n) {:n n}\n270:         (zero? n) :eof\n271:         (native/eintr? e) (recur)\n272:         (native/eagain? e) :would-block\n273:         :else (failure :recv-failed e)))))\n274: \n275: \n276: (defn send-chunk!\n277:   \"One send of `n` bytes from native `buf`: `{:n accepted}` (possibly short,\n278:    possibly 0), `:would-block`, or a failure map (`:error :send-failed`,\n279:    `:class` :broken-pipe or :reset for a peer that has gone). EINTR is\n280:    retried.\"\n281:   [fd buf n]\n282:   (loop []\n283:     (let [[r e] (send-once fd buf n)]\n284:       (cond\n285:         (not (neg? r)) {:n r}\n286:         (native/eintr? e) (recur)\n287:         (native/eagain? e) :would-block\n288:         :else (failure :send-failed e)))))\n289: 4:    listener over the owner-thread pump (`dao.stream.ws.pump`) and the\n10:    One instance per `create` call. Its pump registry, connection records\n13:    instance makes progress only while a driver polls `(host-pump instance)`\n17:    `{:send! :close! :queued-bytes}` (the server's also `:ws/subprotocol`).\n18:    `send!` frames a string as text and host bytes as binary and answers nil\n27:    `(:closed! code reason)`, from the pump's owed terminal, never inside\n28:    `send!` or `close!`; a parser failure over the message bound (1009)\n41:    the pump's 64 KiB read chunk and 16-pong control budget. The pong budget\n46:    it. This side sends no unsolicited pings and ignores pongs.\n57:    forced cleanup after the owner loop has ended: every descriptor closed,\n67:     [dao.stream.ws.pump :as pump]\n92: (defn create\n94:    and `:close-deadline-ms` override the pump defaults for every connection\n98:    {::pump (pump/create)\n107: (defn- st\n112: (defn- live?\n117: (defn- gated\n118:   \"`f` as a pump callback that does nothing once the instance is closed:\n119:    `close-host!` flushes owed pump reports through it without reaching the\n126: (defn- owe!\n134: (defn- deliver-owed!\n142: (defn- forget!\n148: (defn host-pump\n149:   \"The instance as the driver's `:pump` value (A2): the pump's interest and\n150:    deadline (now while this edge owes a report), and `pump!`.\"\n152:   (let [p (::pump inst)]\n153:     {:interest #(pump/interest p)\n154:      :deadline #(if (seq (:owed @(st inst))) (poller/clock-ms) (pump/next-deadline p))\n155:      :pump! (fn [ready]\n157:                     r (pump/pump! p ready)\n166: (defn- protocol\n167:   \"The pump's protocol map for `role` (:server or :client), whose parser\n178: (defn- data-frame\n189: (defn- deliver-message!\n198: (defn- report-closed!\n199:   \"The one terminal of an upgraded connection, from the pump's owed\n208: (defn- seam\n212:   {:send! (fn [payload]\n215:                 (pump/send! p h (data-frame role payload))\n216:                 pump/closed-outcome)))\n219:                (when (= :open phase) (pump/close! p h code reason)))\n221:    :queued-bytes #(if-let [h (: