e guards-off calibration variant of native/jolt-parser and record each nesting shape's stack cost per rule frame and per lookahead link on the 16 MiB parse thread (asserting every bound fits a quarter of the stack; writes build/j5b/calibration.edn), or, with --work, the work metric's per-shape counts and the corpus sweep the work bound derives from (writes build/j5b/work.edn; needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\n63:                          \"src/dev/jolt_j5_calibrate.clj\" *command-line-args*)))}\n65:   probe:jolt-file\n66:   {:doc \"J4a: native/jolt-file gates, each in a child process: JVM-identical frame bytes (both hash algorithms), F2 s32BE prefixes, strict reads, injected short/EINTR/zero-progress/error transfers, corrupt-open byte identity, idempotent close, no fd or native-memory leak, a full collection during a 1 GiB :blocking pwrite, missing/wrong-layout wrapper refused before guest work, exported-symbol allowlist (needs bb build:jolt-native)\"\n68:            (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"bb\" \"native/jolt-file/probes/run.clj\")))}\n70:   probe:jolt-udp\n71:   {:doc \"J0b probe: raw nonblocking SOCK_DGRAM over jolt.ffi on macOS arm64 and Linux x86_64, printing the platform header first (needs bb bootstrap:jolt)\"\n73:            (:exit (shell {:continue true} \"sh\" \"src/dev/jolt_udp_probe.sh\")))}\n75:   probe:jolt-tcp\n76:   {:doc \"J6d: the jolt TCP substrate and owner-thread pump (dao.stream.ws.tcp, dao.stream.ws.pump, driver sleep-fds!), one child jolt process per section: closure (no jolt.socket), address (literals/localhost, resolver trap), substrate (port 0, nonblocking accept/connect, EOF vs reset, gone-peer write survives), ordered (A3 short write, drain order, failure), fairness (A1 ii/iv), stdin (A1 i, held partial line), deadline (A2 seam), control (A3 event orders, A4 pong budget, D1 close slot), close (A5, D2, D3), listener (64 cap, lower-deadlines!, drained?); native memory and registry empty after close. Arguments select sections (needs bb