tery over dao.host.*) and diff the two; writes build/j1-logs/compare-{jvm,jolt}.edn and compare.diff; exit 1 when they differ\"\n216:                          \"mkdir -p build/j1-logs && clojure -M src/dev/jolt_profile_compare.cljc | grep '^\\\\[' > build/j1-logs/compare-jvm.edn && . build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_profile_compare.cljc | grep '^\\\\[' > build/j1-logs/compare-jolt.edn && diff build/j1-logs/compare-jvm.edn build/j1-logs/compare-jolt.edn > build/j1-logs/compare.diff; s=$?; cat build/j1-logs/compare.diff; exit $s\")))}\n218:   test:jolt-host-diag\n219:   {:doc \"J1 DIAGNOSTIC, not the oracle verdict: dao.host.float-test and dao.host.text-test, unchanged, under jolt with the :jolt-diag stand-in for the corpus loader dao.jing.cbor-fixtures (isolates these checks from the real corpus loader); see src/dev/jolt_diag/dao/jing/cbor_fixtures.cljc\"\n222:                          \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-diag:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj dao.host.float-test dao.host.text-test\")))}\n224:   test:jolt-json\n225:   {:doc \"J1: the jolt clojure.data.json shim (src/jolt/clojure/data/json.jolt) against src/dev/jolt_json_shim_check.cljc, under jolt; the same file passes against the real data.json on the JVM (clojure -M:dev, see its header)\"\n228:                          \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj jolt-json-shim-check\")))}\n230:   test:jolt-runner-self\n231:   {:doc \"J1: prove src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj counts a throwing test as one error and keeps running (the jolt-runner-sentinel namespace)\"\n234:                          \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj --self-test\")))}\n236:   jolt:run\n237:   {:doc \"Run the bootstrapped jolt with build/tools/jolt-env.sh, passing every argument