{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"The guards now cover both zero-byte sends and repeated `:would-block` results. I also fixed a separate short-write defect: `write-all!` advanced its counter but resent from byte zero.\n\nThe task now uses a supervisor that counts completed B replies, flushes running telemetry every ten seconds, and kills the worker at five minutes with a FAILURE report. First-round phase markers should identify which call fails to return if the initial spin recurs. Verification is still limited to static review, as requested."}}
